 p/san-jose\n\nWorld Arts West Dance Festival returns to Presidio Tunnel To
 ps on Sunday\, September 6 th from 1-4pm. Come out to the park for an afte
 rnoon of dance workshops and performances. Bring family and friends\, a bl
 anket and picnic\, or walk over to Presidio Pop Up’s to purchase delicio
 us food celebrating the Bay Area’s diverse cuisines. This event is part 
 of a three-weekend festival that includes film screenings and other commun
 ity activations rooted in this year’s theme\, “ Legacy of Liberation 
 ” – a theme which addresses the holistic needs of the community. World
  Arts West isn’t just providing visibility to artists but also economic 
 empowerment\, cultural preservation\, and collective advocacy. See all the
  World Arts West Dance Festival activations this year . Weekend Three in t
 he park will feature live dance performances by Academy of Danse Libre \, 
 Amazed by Grace Dance Ministry\, Los Lupeños de San José and Uzumaru . D
 ancers Tainah Damasceno and LaKiesha Golden will also lead us in community
  Brazilian Line dances for the whole family to join!
